================================================================================
Clean-room statement
================================================================================
OpenOSV was written without access to DJI source code.  The .OSV container
layout, the protobuf field numbering of the per-frame metadata and the lens
calibration model were determined by inspecting recorded files and publicly
documented interfaces.  No DJI binaries, resources (masks, remap tables, neural
network models, LUT images) or SDK headers are included in this repository or
in the distributed binaries.

================================================================================
Colour science provenance
================================================================================
* BT.2100 HLG / PQ transfer functions, BT.2020 and BT.709 primaries and the
  BT.2408 signal-level anchors are implemented from the public ITU-R
  Recommendations BT.2100-2, BT.2020-2, BT.709-6, BT.2408-5 and BT.2390-8.
* The "DJI-matched" D-Log M decoding curve is an analytic 7-parameter fit
  produced by scripts/fit_dlogm.py from 64 neutral-axis measurements of DJI's
  publicly distributed D-Log M to HLG rendering.  Only the fitted constants and
  the measurement table are shipped; no DJI LUT data is redistributed.
* The "Osmo 360" D-Log M decoding curve (the default) is an analytic
  7-parameter fit of the same form, produced by
  `scripts/fit_dlogm.py --from-cube DJI_Osmo360_DLogM_to_Rec709.cube` from the
  33 neutral-axis (R == G == B) samples of DJI's publicly distributed Osmo 360
  D-Log M to Rec.709 LUT.  Measuring a transfer function is what was done, not
  copying a table: what is shipped is the seven fitted constants
  (include/osv/color/DlogM.h) and the 33 measured diagonal values recorded as
  the fit's provenance and residual reference (scripts/fit_dlogm.py,
  tests/unit/test_color.cpp).  No DJI LUT data is redistributed, and none of
  the .cube files in luts/ contains any: each is generated in full by
  `osvtool lut` from OpenOSV's own fitted curve and transfer functions
  (scripts/gen_luts.ps1 regenerates them reproducibly).
* The "Pocket 3" D-Log M curve reproduces the numeric constants of the publicly
  published community fit by Thatcher Freeman (github.com/thatcherfreeman/
  dwg-transforms).  The constants are facts about a transfer function; no source
  code from that repository is included.

